#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# equal

#% text
# `equal(a, b)`, written `a == b`, gives `true` or `false` when the comparison can be decided, and stays as an equation otherwise.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Numbers compare by value: `1 == 1.0` is `true`.

#% item
# An equation that stays symbolic is what `solve` and the other equation functions take.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
2 + 2 == 4
#% output
#= true

#% cell
1 == 1.0
#% output
#= true

#% cell
x^2 == 4
#% output
#= x^2 == 4

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Equations as values:

#% cell
solve(x^2 == 4, x)
#% output
#= [[x -> -2], [x -> 2]]

#% text
# Use `same` for an always decided structural test:

#% cell
[x == y, same(x, y)]
#% output
#= [x == y, false]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Truth values and algebraic numbers:

#% cell
[true == false, sqrt(2) + sqrt(3) == sqrt(5 + 2*sqrt(6))]
#% output
#= [false, true]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `same`, `unequal`, `solve`, `less`
